# Auto-commit & push to Gitea

After completing user-requested code/config/docs changes in `/var/www/lab-console`, **automatically** commit and push to Gitea unless the user opted out.

## Skip when

User explicitly says not to commit/push, e.g. `ne pas pousser`, `sans commit`, `sans publier`, `don't push`.

## Repo

- Path: `/var/www/lab-console`
- Remote: `git@git.aguilera.ch:Aguilera_lab/AzureLabs.git`
- Web: https://git.aguilera.ch/Aguilera_Lab/AzureLabs
- Branch: `main`

Prefer: `./scripts/push_to_gitea.sh "<message>"` when the script exists.

## Git wrapper (dubious ownership)

```bash
GIT_CONFIG_GLOBAL=/dev/null git -c safe.directory=/var/www/lab-console -C /var/www/lab-console <args>
```

## Procedure

1. In parallel: `status`, `diff` (staged+unstaged), `log -5 --oneline`
2. If no real changes → do not create an empty commit; tell the user
3. Fix origin if wrong:
   `remote set-url origin git@git.aguilera.ch:Aguilera_lab/AzureLabs.git`
4. Stage relevant files only. **Never** stage: `backend/.env`, `data/*`, secrets, tokens, credentials
5. Commit via HEREDOC (clear why-focused message):

```bash
git commit -m "$(cat <<'EOF'
Your message here.

EOF
)"
```

6. Push `origin main` (SSH first). **No** `--force`. **No** amend unless user commit rules allow
7. If SSH auth fails, retry HTTPS (`https://git.aguilera.ch/Aguilera_Lab/AzureLabs.git`) using env/`gh`/ask — **never** hardcode or write tokens into files
8. Confirm briefly: short hash + pushed to Gitea `Aguilera_lab/AzureLabs` (`main`)
